WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.780
Finish a thread with a pull request and auto-merge.

2
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.585
In greet-app, the coordinator started a thread, Greet a team, in its own worktree.

3
00:00:10.585 --> 00:00:17.703
Codex does T-01 of increment 0002, commits, and stops with a clean tree.

4
00:00:17.703 --> 00:00:24.190
Then the project's finish rule runs: SpecWithCode opens pull request #2 into main,

5
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.795
and turns on auto-merge.

6
00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:31.630
But main changed the same lines, so the thread reports a conflict and does not merge.

7
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.439
The rule is a project setting: When a thread finishes, Open PR and auto-merge.

8
00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:41.990
This project squashes on merge and removes agent credit lines.

9
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.221
Code Review shows the pull request blocked by the conflict, with auto-merge armed.

10
00:00:47.221 --> 00:00:52.620
No review is required in this repo. The Code tab shows the thread's change.

11
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.179
Send the conflict back to the thread that wrote the code.

12
00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:03.600
Codex merges main, keeps the new Hi wording for teams, runs npm test, and pushes.

13
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.431
Auto-merge is still on. The required test check passes, and GitHub merges it.

14
00:01:09.431 --> 00:01:13.160
The thread shows Merged #2 into main.

15
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:18.110
Next, sw-done verifies and closes the increment.
